Do not let an ACDB failure leave the phone mute

q6core_probe returned the result of loading the ACDB, so any stumble there
brought down q6core's probe and with it THE WHOLE AUDIO CHAIN: the phone
booted with "--- no soundcards ---", PulseAudio on auto_null and not a single
device on the apr bus (no q6afe, no q6routing, nothing).

It happened on 2026-08-11 while trying surya's own ACDB, and it left the phone
completely mute until the previous one was put back.

Registering the topologies is OPTIONAL: it serves the audio of calls, and
without it everything else works just the same. It has no right whatsoever to
take the sound card down with it.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6core.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6core.c
@@ -501,7 +501,17 @@
 	g_core->adev = adev;
 	init_waitqueue_head(&g_core->wait);
 
-	return q6core_load_and_register_topologies(&adev->dev);
+	/*
+	 * The result is ignored ON PURPOSE. Registering the topologies is
+	 * OPTIONAL: it is needed for calls, and without it the rest of the audio
+	 * works the same. Returning it made any stumble loading the
+	 * ACDB take down the q6core probe and with it the WHOLE audio chain:
+	 * the phone booted with "--- no soundcards ---" and not a single device
+	 * on the apr bus. It happened on 2026-08-11 and left the phone mute.
+	 */
+	q6core_load_and_register_topologies(&adev->dev);
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static void q6core_exit(struct apr_device *adev)
